cartridge "FIREDAMP/AMY & CLAUDE/2026"

' FIREDAMP - an original game by Amy & Claude for Amy Studio, 2026, in Amy.
' (working title GEM MINE; folder games/gemmine)
'
' A real-time descent through eight deep mines (14 x 60 cells of 16 x 16
' px, a smooth vertical scroll over four and a half screens each). Dig down
' to the lift at the bottom; it opens when enough gems are found. Rocks
' fall when what holds them is dug away and roll off other rocks: cave-ins
' run as chain reactions over the whole mine. Green gas pockets are
' firedamp: dig one and the lamp lights it, BOOM one second later (3 x 3,
' it lights the gas next to it): blasts clear rock and dirt, open new ways
' and set off new cave-ins. The lamp burns oil (the timer); each gem adds
' oil. Three timber beams a mine: the button sets one in the miner's cell;
' a beam holds up the rocks above it and is a ladder.
'
' Controls: stick left/right walk, dig, push a rock (one cell, when the
' cell beyond is empty); down digs; up digs the cell above, or climbs a
' beam; up+left/right steps up onto a one-cell ledge. Button (either):
' set a beam. Hold the button 2 s: give up this attempt (a life).
' Liberties: none (original). Not a clone: no enemies, the miner has
' gravity (side view), beams, firedamp blasts, oil, a scrolling descent.
'
' CREDITS CONVENTION: original game made together (see CreditsPage).
'
' --- engine (asm, below) ---------------------------------------------------
' VRAM in play: patterns $0000 and colours $2000 shared by the three thirds
' (R4 = 0, R3 = $9F), 247 codes: code 0 black, scroll combos (art.py: every
' (cell half above, cell half below, column) pair pre-drawn at shifts 0, 2,
' 4, 6), two pools of 6 dig tiles, HUD icons. Name pages $1800 and $1C00
' (R2 6/7), sprites $1B00 / $3800. The MAP lives in VRAM at $0800 (row r,
' column c at $0800 + 16r + c; one byte a cell = its kind): 1 KB of RAM
' would not hold it.
' A tick = 2 frames. Frame A (vblank): flip R2 to the page built during the
' last tick + its sprite table; input, logic tick (as model.mjs), physics
' chunk, camera, map window (11 rows of the map read to RAM as visual
' kinds), names of screen rows 2-11 into the hidden page. Frame B: names
' of rows 12-21 + HUD, dig tiles (the cell being dug, crumbling, drawn into
' 6 pool tiles), sprites, physics chunk. Physics: 4 map rows a frame
' bottom-up, the whole mine every 15 frames (one cell of fall a sweep).
' The camera moves 2 px a tick at most.

